WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.100
Hi, you guys.
大家好。

9
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.760
We're really excited today.
我们今天真的很兴奋。

10
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.820
We're so excited.
我们太兴奋了。

11
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.060
We can't wait to share this episode with you.
我们迫不及待想和你们分享这一集了。

12
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.220
This episode's all about The Office BFFs, our book, because...
这一集的主题是关于我们的书《办公室死党》，因为……

13
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.040
We are in New York City right now for the launch of our book.
我们现在正在纽约市，为我们的新书发布做准备。

14
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.560
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

15
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.460
This has been such a long journey.
这一路走来真的很漫长。

16
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.620
You guys have been with us every step of the way, truly.
你们真的全程陪伴着我们。

17
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.840
Yes, your support means so much to us.
是的，你们的支持对我们意义重大。

18
00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.940
And Jenna and I were talking about reading part of our book or sharing part of our book and where we would do that.
珍娜和我之前在讨论要读一读我们的书，或者分享书里的内容，还在想在哪里进行比较好。

19
00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.920
And we were both immediately like, we have to share it with our office ladies' family firSt.
我们俩当时立刻就说，我们必须先和“办公室女士”大家庭分享。

20
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.920
And you guys sent in so many great questions about the book.
你们寄来了很多关于这本书的好问题。

21
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.300
We're going to answer them today.
我们今天会一一解答。

22
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.400
You know, we've been doing a bunch of press for the book, and one of the things I did was the Goal Digger podcaSt.
你知道，我们最近为这本书做了很多宣传，其中我参加了《Goal Digger》播客。

23
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.720
Oh, you loved that one.
哦，你很喜欢那一期。

24
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:15.060
I loved it with Jenna Kutcher.
我很喜欢和珍娜·库彻的那次交流。

25
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.680
And you know what she said to me, Ange?
你知道她跟我说了什么吗，安吉？

26
00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.260
We keep saying launch of our book.
我们一直说“新书发布”。

27
00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:21.640
And she said, do you know why it's called a book release?
她说，你知道为什么叫“书的释放”（book release）吗？

28
00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:22.460
Why?
为什么？

29
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.260
That's what I said.
我当时就是这么问的。

30
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:23.880
I was like, why?
我当时问，为什么？

31
00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.860
And she said, because you release your work into the world.
她说，因为你要把你的作品释放到世界上。

32
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:30.880
And you let it go.
你要放手。

33
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.100
You have to let it go.
你必须放手。

34
00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.100
You work on it.
你为它付出了努力。

35
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.780
You make it the best it can be.
你把它打磨到极致。

36
00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:36.800
And then you release it.
然后你释放它。

37
00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.420
And you have to release it.
你必须释放它。

38
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.000
You have to let it out.
你必须把它放出来。

39
00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:40.660
Let it go.
放手吧。

40
00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.400
Oh, I love that.
哦，我喜欢这个说法。

41
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:42.760
Right?
对吧？

42
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:44.300
I did.
我当时也是这么想的。

43
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:44.860
Me too.
我也是。

44
00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:45.480
I love that.
我很喜欢。

45
00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:51.220
Well, you know, even though this is a special episode of Office Ladies, we still have to have fast facts.
好吧，你知道，尽管这是《办公室女士》的特别节目，我们还是得有“快速事实”环节。

46
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:52.500
I need my structure.
我需要我的结构感。

47
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.140
You know me.
你了解我的。

48
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.760
Are you going to do a summary too?
你也要做剧情梗概吗？

49
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.760
Oh, I didn't write a summary.
哦，我没写梗概。

50
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.040
Sorry to disappoint.
抱歉让你失望了。

51
00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.420
Let's do fast facts.
我们来快速了解一些事实吧。

52
00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.200
I have one.
我有一个。

53
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.040
Our book was printed in Willard, Ohio.
我们的书是在俄亥俄州的威拉德印刷的。

54
00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.200
Hey.
嘿。

55
00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:12.360
And I thought, well, gee, if our book was printed in Willard, Ohio, I want to know a little bit about Willard, Ohio.
我就想，哎呀，既然我们的书是在俄亥俄州的威拉德印刷的，那我想多了解一下威拉德这个地方。

56
00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:13.160
What you got?
你有什么发现？

57
00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.440
Here's what I got.
这是我的发现。

58
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.320
I went to their official city website, www.willardohio.us.
我访问了他们的城市官网，www.willardohio.us。

59
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:21.480
Here are things I wanted to share.
以下是我想要分享的内容。

60
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:33.820
The town was founded in 1874, but it was named Chicago because it was the train junction for the Baltimore and Ohio railroads line to Sandusky and the branch west to Chicago.
该镇始建于1874年，当时被命名为芝加哥，因为它是巴尔的摩与俄亥俄铁路通往桑达斯基的线路以及向西通往芝加哥的分支线路的交汇点。

61
00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.340
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

62
00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:35.860
What?
怎么了？

63
00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.380
People would get confused.
人们会感到困惑。

64
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.740
I would get confused.
我也会感到困惑。

65
00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:42.480
I would be on the train and I would be like, did I make it to Chicago?
如果我在火车上，我会想，我是不是到芝加哥了？

66
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:43.300
Illinois?
伊利诺伊州的那个？

67
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.420
And they would say, yes, but I wasn't in Chicago, Chicago.
他们会说是，但我其实并不在真正的芝加哥。

68
00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.440
You were in Chicago, Ohio.
你是在俄亥俄州的芝加哥。

69
00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.640
I think I would still be confused as a traveler.
我觉得作为一名旅客，我还是会感到困惑。

70
00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.120
I have to be honest with you.
老实说。

71
00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:09.620
In 1917, to finally rectify the confusion, the town changed its name to Willard after the then president of the Baltimore and Ohio Railroad Company, Daniel Willard.
1917年，为了彻底消除这种困惑，该镇以时任巴尔的摩与俄亥俄铁路公司总裁丹尼尔·威拉德的名字，更名为威拉德。

72
00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.800
And then Willard became an official city in 1960.
后来威拉德在1960年正式成为一座城市。

73
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:20.600
Population as of 2019, 60, and here are a few things from their website.
截至2019年的人口数据是60人，以下是他们网站上的一些信息。

74
00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:23.860
Their slogan is, proud to call Willard home.
他们的口号是：以威拉德为家，引以为豪。

75
00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.120
Listen to how they describe their city.
听听他们是怎么描述自己城市的。

76
00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:34.020
A community where people enjoy living and working, ideally situated with easy access to Ohio's interstates and rail lines.
一个人们乐于在此生活和工作的社区，地理位置优越，可轻松前往俄亥俄州的州际公路和铁路线。

77
00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:37.420
Willard is in the heart of the Midwest manufacturing region.
威拉德位于中西部制造业中心地带。

78
00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:45.260
Abundant land and utilities, a solid work ethic, and a progressive local government make Willard the perfect choice for growing a business.
充足的土地和公用设施、扎实的职业道德以及进步的地方政府，使威拉德成为企业发展的理想选择。

79
00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:46.520
We have to go.
我们得去一趟。

80
00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:47.520
We have to go.
我们得去一趟。

81
00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:51.320
Not only that, here are a few things that are happening just this month in Willard.
不仅如此，以下是威拉德这个月正在举办的一些活动。

82
00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.560
They honor their hometown heroes.
他们会表彰家乡英雄。

83
00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.740
They started doing this in 2018.
这项活动始于2018年。

84
00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:04.060
Each week, a different hometown hero will be recognized on the electric sign at the Willard City Park, as well as through the city's Facebook page.
每周，一位不同的家乡英雄都会在威拉德城市公园的电子显示屏上，以及通过该市的Facebook页面获得表彰。

85
00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.060
Very good.
非常好。

86
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.180
They have the Willard Tree Program.
他们还有威拉德植树计划。

87
00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:15.340
In partnership with the Willard Moose Lodge 2153, the city of Willard is offering a tree planting program to help property owners plant trees.
威拉德市与威拉德第2153号驼鹿会分会合作，提供植树计划，帮助业主种植树木。

88
00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.660
They also have the Downtown Spring Festival.
他们还有市中心春季艺术节。

89
00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.040
It's returning this year, featuring the mother of all pickleball tournaments.
今年将回归，届时会有规模空前的匹克球锦标赛。

90
00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.140
I love pickleball!
我爱匹克球！

91
00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:25.800
I know, wait.
我知道，等等。

92
00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:31.000
Cornhole, craft vendors, touch a truck, bike rodeo, and more.
还有玉米洞游戏、手工艺品摊位、触摸卡车体验、自行车竞技表演等等。

93
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.380
Angela, it's becoming very clear to me that we need to go to Willard, Ohio.
安吉拉，我很清楚我们需要去一趟俄亥俄州的威拉德了。

94
00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.160
I know!
我知道！

95
00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.320
And that's where our book was printed.
而且我们的书就是在那儿印刷的。

96
00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.020
Thank you, Willard, Ohio!
谢谢你，俄亥俄州的威拉德！

97
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.300
Thank you, Willard, Ohio!
谢谢你，俄亥俄州的威拉德！

98
00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:43.060
I also have a few book stats.
我还有一些关于书的数据。

99
00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:43.620
Oh!
哦！

100
00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.100
Well, you know I love stats.
好吧，你知道我喜欢数据。

101
00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.280
You and Dr. Thibodeau.
你和蒂博多医生。

102
00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:46.920
Yes.
是的。

103
00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:51.420
Here are all of our The Office BFF's book stats.
这是我们《办公室死党》一书的所有数据统计。

104
00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.300
There are 336 pages in our book.
我们的书共有336页。

105
00:04:55.940 --> 00:05:00.440
There are 440 photos or images in the interior.
内页里有440张照片或图片。

106
00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:01.940
440, Jenna.
440张，珍娜。

107
00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.240
So there are more photos than pages.
所以照片比页数还多。

108
00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:09.280
There are 16 photos in the end papers.
环衬页上有16张照片。

109
00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.080
Okay, so I did not know what end papers were until we started making this book.
好吧，在开始制作这本书之前，我根本不知道什么是环衬页。

110
00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.080
That's the part of the book where you open it up and it's like...
就是你打开书的那一部分，就像是……

111
00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:19.780
Part of the cover.
封面的一部分。

112
00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.100
Right, it's the back of the cover and then the next little page.
没错，就是封面的背面以及紧接着的那一小页。

113
00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.780
And we put all of these amazing black and white photos from the show.
我们在那里放了所有来自剧组的精彩黑白照片。

114
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.180
I love the end papers.
我超爱这些环衬页。

115
00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.060
They're so special.
它们太特别了。

116
00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:35.460
That we took, by the way, all the photos in the book are personal photos or photos that
顺便说一下，书里所有的照片都是我们自己拍的，或者是

117
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.720
were shared with us from our friends on the show.
剧组朋友们分享给我们的。

118
00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.260
Yes.
没错。

119
00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:40.720
Here's another stat I love.
这里还有另一个我喜欢的数据。

120
00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:44.820
There are 41 pieces of memorabilia in the book.
书里有41件纪念品。

121
00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:51.280
That includes ticket stubs, fan art, posters, brochures, photos of papers and objects and
其中包括票根、粉丝艺术作品、海报、宣传册、文件和物品的照片以及

122
00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:51.680
sketches.
草图。

123
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.500
All of these things we saved over the years from the show.
这些都是我们多年来从剧组保存下来的东西。

124
00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.280
So one of the pieces of memorabilia is in my chapter, Jam.
其中一件纪念品就在我的章节“Jam”里。

125
00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.020
I have a chapter where I wrote all about Jim and Pam.
我有一个专门写吉姆和帕姆的章节。

126
00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:08.060
Lee, my husband, saved his lactation consultant badge.
我丈夫李保存了他的哺乳顾问胸牌。

127
00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:08.980
As the nurse.
作为护士的那个。

128
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.660
As the lactation nurse.
作为哺乳护士的那个。

129
00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:12.880
And we scanned it and put it in the book.
我们把它扫描下来放进了书里。

130
00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:13.640
Love it.
太棒了。

131
00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:18.140
But a lot of you wrote in and asked us where all the book will be sold.
但你们很多人写信问我们这本书会在哪里发售。

132
00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:18.820
What countries?
哪些国家？

133
00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:25.100
We don't have a precise number yet, but definitely United States, Canada, and the UK, as well
我们目前还没有确切的数字，但肯定包括美国、加拿大和英国，以及

134
00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.980
as various English-speaking countries.
其他各个英语国家。

135
00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.440
But as soon as I know all of those countries, I'm going to let you know.
一旦我知道所有这些国家，我会第一时间告诉你们。

136
00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:33.140
The book is also going to be translated into other languages.
这本书也会被翻译成其他语言。

137
00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.860
And as we know where it will be coming out, we'll let you know.
一旦我们知道会在哪些地方发行，我们会通知你们。

138
00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.320
Well, lady, my fast fact number two is all about the audiobook.
好吧，女士，我的第二个快速事实是关于有声书的。

139
00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:48.020
We got a lot of people who asked, does the audiobook come with access to those 440 photos?
很多人问，有声书是否包含那440张照片的访问权限？

140
00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:49.360
No.
没有。

141
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.360
No, we do not have one of those supplemental PDFs that you sometimes get with an audiobook.
没有，我们没有提供那种有时会随有声书附赠的补充PDF文件。

142
00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:00.440
But we have a bunch of fun audio surprises.
但我们准备了一堆有趣的音频惊喜。

143
00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:05.040
So many cool people really showed up for us for this audiobook.
很多很酷的人真的为我们的有声书捧场了。

144
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:05.800
They did.
他们确实来了。

145
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:12.000
Creed Bratton wrote an Office BFFs song for us, which we used to kick it off.
克里德·布拉顿为我们写了一首《办公室死党》之歌，我们用它作为开场。

146
00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.860
It makes me happy every time I hear it.
每次听到它我都觉得很开心。

147
00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:14.560
I love it.
我超爱它。

148
00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:20.480
Rainn Wilson wrote and reads a special foreword that is exclusive to the audiobook.
雷恩·威尔逊写了一篇特别的前言并亲自朗读，这是有声书独有的。

149
00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:23.020
You can't even read it in the hardcopy book.
你在纸质书里甚至都读不到。

150
