759
00:35:06.460 --> 00:35:07.500
They're not stylized.
它们没有经过刻意修饰。

760
00:35:07.600 --> 00:35:08.400
There are pictures.
就是一些生活照。

761
00:35:08.400 --> 00:35:11.740
So in one of them, and Jenna knows the one I'm talking about, we're having lunch in
其中有一张，Jenna知道我说的是哪一张，当时我们正在她的

762
00:35:11.740 --> 00:35:12.140
her trailer.
拖车里吃午饭。

763
00:35:12.340 --> 00:35:13.620
My eyes aren't fully open.
我的眼睛都没完全睁开。

764
00:35:14.300 --> 00:35:16.120
It is not an attractive picture.
那照片拍得一点也不好看。

765
00:35:16.360 --> 00:35:17.300
It's in the book.
但它被收录在书里了。

766
00:35:17.300 --> 00:35:20.400
But it's the only one we had of us eating lunch together.
因为那是我们唯一一张一起吃午饭的照片。

767
00:35:20.580 --> 00:35:21.200
In your trailer.
在你的拖车里。

768
00:35:21.420 --> 00:35:21.900
In my trailer.
在我的拖车里。

769
00:35:22.240 --> 00:35:24.440
So I was like, it's got to go in the book.
所以我当时就想，它一定要放进书里。

770
00:35:24.540 --> 00:35:25.620
It helps tell the story.
它有助于讲述我们的故事。

771
00:35:25.980 --> 00:35:31.500
But in addition to the photos, one of the things I love are some of the sketches that made it
除了照片，我最喜欢的部分之一是书中收录的一些草图，比如我画了一只小猫，邀请大家参加Sprinkles生日派对的

772
00:35:31.500 --> 00:35:38.260
in, my post-it note where I drew a little cat and invited everyone to Sprinkles' birthday party
便利贴，

773
00:35:38.260 --> 00:35:40.540
in the parking lot is in the book.
就在停车场，也被收录在书里了。

774
00:35:40.560 --> 00:35:40.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

775
00:35:41.100 --> 00:35:42.240
The original one.
原件哦。

776
00:35:42.580 --> 00:35:49.860
Well, my favorite photo in the book, I just realized, was my favorite when we did our very
嗯，我刚意识到，我书里最喜欢的一张照片，是在我们做最后一次

777
00:35:49.860 --> 00:35:53.980
last pass of the book because I noticed a detail about it.
校对时才发现的，因为我注意到了一个细节。

778
00:35:54.220 --> 00:35:54.480
What?
什么？

779
00:35:54.760 --> 00:36:00.900
There is a picture of Angela in curlers sitting on the steps of her trailer.
有一张Angela戴着卷发筒坐在拖车台阶上的照片。

780
00:36:01.500 --> 00:36:04.600
And if you look closely, she's got half a donut in her hand.
如果你仔细看，她手里拿着半个甜甜圈。

781
00:36:04.700 --> 00:36:07.920
And we didn't notice that for two years.
我们竟然两年都没发现。

782
00:36:07.920 --> 00:36:08.640
We did not notice the donut.
我们完全没注意到那个甜甜圈。

783
00:36:08.720 --> 00:36:10.300
Two years of looking at layouts.
看了两年的排版。

784
00:36:10.300 --> 00:36:14.880
It wasn't until the final pass, I was like, oh my God, I'm holding a donut.
直到最后一次校对，我才惊呼，天哪，我手里拿着个甜甜圈。

785
00:36:15.380 --> 00:36:17.420
It's officially my favorite picture.
它正式成为我最喜欢的照片了。

786
00:36:19.100 --> 00:36:19.800
All right.
好吧。

787
00:36:19.880 --> 00:36:22.880
We also got a question from Amro in Palestine.
我们还收到了来自巴勒斯坦的Amro的一个问题。

788
00:36:23.220 --> 00:36:29.300
Were there any specific moments that made you emotional to recall when you were writing them?
在写书的时候，有没有哪些特定的时刻让你回忆起来感到情绪激动？

789
00:36:29.300 --> 00:36:35.500
I actually cried writing the story about my dad because my dad has passed away.
写到关于我父亲的故事时，我确实哭了，因为我父亲已经去世了。

790
00:36:35.840 --> 00:36:40.920
And just remembering taking him with me to the Emmys, look, I'll cry right now, you know?
仅仅是回忆起带他去参加艾美奖，看，我现在都要哭了，你知道吗？

791
00:36:41.200 --> 00:36:43.880
It was just really special that he got to go with me.
他能陪我一起去，这真的非常特别。

792
00:36:43.920 --> 00:36:45.600
And I love that I can share that.
我很庆幸能把这段经历分享出来。

793
00:36:46.300 --> 00:36:52.440
And also just reliving what it was like to be in an award show through my dad's eyes also tickled me.
而且，通过我父亲的视角重温颁奖典礼的经历也让我觉得很有趣。

794
00:36:52.440 --> 00:36:58.800
Because he had some really funny sidebar commentary because he was a little confused about what all was happening.
因为他当时有一些非常搞笑的旁白评论，因为他不太明白到底发生了什么。

795
00:36:59.040 --> 00:37:01.260
It just really means a lot to me that that's in the book.
能把这些写进书里，对我来说意义重大。

796
00:37:01.680 --> 00:37:06.560
Well, there's a chapter in the book called Big Pregs, Little Pregs, Fake Pregs.
嗯，书里有一个章节叫《大孕、小孕、假孕》。

797
00:37:06.660 --> 00:37:16.000
And that chapter is all about our time being both real and fake pregnant on The Office and in real life.
那一章讲的都是我们在《办公室》剧组和现实生活中，真实怀孕和假装怀孕的那段时光。

798
00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:20.640
We share about what our friendship went through when we became moMs.
我们分享了当我们成为妈妈后，我们的友谊经历了怎样的变化。

799
00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:32.380
And in that section, I share about going back to work five weeks after having my son, which was a C-section.
在那一部分，我分享了自己在剖腹产五周后就重返工作岗位的经历。

800
00:37:32.820 --> 00:37:39.440
And I was not physically or emotionally ready to go back to work.
当时我在身体和心理上都还没准备好回去工作。

801
00:37:39.440 --> 00:37:46.020
And I explain sort of why I had to go back to work after such a short period of time in the book.
我在书中解释了为什么我在那么短的时间后就不得不回去工作。

802
00:37:46.360 --> 00:37:51.680
But I also share about what Angela did to support me through that time.
但我也分享了安吉拉在那段时间里是如何支持我的。

803
00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:59.900
And it was really emotional for me to recall that time because I was struggling.
回想起那段时光对我来说真的很感性，因为当时我正处于挣扎之中。

804
00:38:00.800 --> 00:38:07.620
And so that was a very vulnerable process for you to just remember it all and put it back down on the page.
所以对你来说，要把这一切都回忆起来并写在纸上，是一个非常脆弱的过程。

805
00:38:07.800 --> 00:38:08.140
Yeah.
是的。

806
00:38:08.140 --> 00:38:11.280
To kind of have to access that again.
不得不重新去触碰那些记忆。

807
00:38:11.620 --> 00:38:14.300
But I'm so glad we shared about it, though.
但我很高兴我们分享了这些。

808
00:38:14.760 --> 00:38:15.540
Me too.
我也是。

809
00:38:15.540 --> 00:38:18.240
It was actually very healing, I have to say.
我必须说，这实际上非常有治愈作用。

810
00:38:18.440 --> 00:38:22.020
I think because I got to recall all that support as well.
我想是因为我也得以回想起当时所获得的所有支持。

811
00:38:22.400 --> 00:38:22.660
Yeah.
是的。

812
00:38:23.180 --> 00:38:25.940
Well, Miguel from Mexico sent in this question.
好的，来自墨西哥的米格尔发来了这个问题。

813
00:38:26.420 --> 00:38:31.460
Miguel says, we're familiar with your process to deep dive and source from your journals.
米格尔说，我们很熟悉你深入挖掘并从日记中寻找素材的过程。

814
00:38:31.660 --> 00:38:34.400
But still, how can you remember so much?
但即便如此，你是怎么能记住那么多的？

815
00:38:34.400 --> 00:38:38.820
Well, Miguel, we have a lot of people who help us out.
嗯，米格尔，我们有很多人的帮助。

816
00:38:39.440 --> 00:38:47.640
For example, with this book, we did long interviews with our hairstylist, Kim Ferry, our costume designer, Carrie Bennett.
例如，在写这本书时，我们采访了我们的发型师金·费里和服装设计师凯莉·贝内特。

817
00:38:47.640 --> 00:38:56.840
I traded a gazillion emails with Randy Cordray and James Carey when I was writing about going to Niagara.
当我在写关于去尼亚加拉瀑布的内容时，我和兰迪·科德雷以及詹姆斯·凯里交换了无数封邮件。

818
00:38:57.180 --> 00:38:57.260
Yeah.
是的。

819
00:38:57.260 --> 00:39:02.360
And James and Randy shared photos that they had taken.
詹姆斯和兰迪分享了他们当时拍的照片。

820
00:39:02.360 --> 00:39:06.060
And guys, the photos in this book, you have never seen them.
伙计们，这本书里的照片，你们绝对没见过。

821
00:39:06.180 --> 00:39:11.040
James Carey has a photo of all of us in our blue parkas on Maid of the MiSt.
詹姆斯·凯里有一张我们所有人穿着蓝色派克大衣在“雾中少女号”上的照片。

822
00:39:11.760 --> 00:39:23.680
Randy has a photo that John and I took as Jim and Pam holding up our hands with our wedding rings on right after we did the marriage scene on the Maid of the MiSt.
兰迪有一张照片，是约翰和我以吉姆和帕姆的身份，在“雾中少女号”上拍完结婚场景后，举起戴着婚戒的手拍的。

823
00:39:23.680 --> 00:39:25.580
I'd never seen that photo before.
我以前从没见过那张照片。

824
00:39:25.720 --> 00:39:28.000
I said, oh, Randy, can I put that in the book?
我说，噢，兰迪，我可以把它放进书里吗？

825
00:39:28.080 --> 00:39:29.000
And he said yes.
他说可以。

826
00:39:29.480 --> 00:39:29.920
Amazing.
太棒了。

827
00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:32.840
Same with our producer, Steve Burgess.
我们的制片人史蒂夫·伯吉斯也是一样。

828
00:39:33.000 --> 00:39:37.380
I was trading all of these emails with him about the finale, remembering all the details.
我当时和他交换了所有关于大结局的邮件，回忆起所有的细节。

829
00:39:37.700 --> 00:39:44.740
And he had a photo from our final table read from a different angle that showed the whole room that I'd never seen before.
他有一张我们最后一次剧本围读的照片，是从另一个角度拍的，展示了整个房间，我以前从未见过。

830
00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:47.200
He graciously let us put it in the book.
他慷慨地让我们把它放进了书里。

831
00:39:47.340 --> 00:39:48.220
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

832
00:39:53.680 --> 00:39:57.120
We got some photos of things that we didn't have in our personal collection.
我们得到了一些我们个人收藏中没有的照片。

833
00:39:57.520 --> 00:40:01.580
And looking through some of his photos jogged so many memories.
翻看他的一些照片勾起了我许多回忆。

834
00:40:01.960 --> 00:40:02.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

835
00:40:02.540 --> 00:40:03.700
He was amazing.
他太棒了。

836
00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:04.360
Yes.
是的。

837
00:40:04.520 --> 00:40:06.100
And we included a few of his.
我们收录了他的一些照片。

838
00:40:06.320 --> 00:40:09.380
Aaron Schur, Kent Sabornak, Alicia Raycraft.
亚伦·舒尔、肯特·萨博纳克、艾丽西亚·雷克拉夫特。

839
00:40:09.580 --> 00:40:10.540
Greg Daniels.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

840
00:40:10.760 --> 00:40:11.880
Ken Kwapis.
肯·卡皮斯。

841
00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:15.620
I mean, guys, we cannot thank you enough for your support.
我是说，伙计们，我们对你们的支持感激不尽。

842
00:40:15.620 --> 00:40:16.440
But that's how.
这就是方法。

843
00:40:16.580 --> 00:40:18.600
It's not just our memories and our journals.
这不仅仅是靠我们的记忆和日记。

844
00:40:18.600 --> 00:40:25.040
It is the relationships we have with other people and their willingness to share their memories with us.
更是靠我们与他人的关系，以及他们愿意与我们分享他们的记忆。

845
00:40:25.280 --> 00:40:27.140
That's how we remember so much.
这就是我们能记住那么多的原因。

846
00:40:27.660 --> 00:40:28.140
100%.
百分之百。

847
00:40:28.140 --> 00:40:33.800
Kate Flannery and I, bless her heart, I can't even tell you how many crazy texts I sent her.
凯特·弗兰纳里和我，愿上帝保佑她，我甚至无法告诉你我给她发了多少疯狂的短信。

848
00:40:34.280 --> 00:40:38.100
Like, Kate, do you remember at the award show when we pretended to have a fake fight?
比如，凯特，你还记得在颁奖典礼上我们假装吵架的时候吗？

849
00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:39.640
Oh, yeah.
噢，记得。

850
00:40:39.640 --> 00:40:40.580
We put that in the book.
我们把它写进书里了。

851
00:40:40.720 --> 00:40:44.680
I found all our photos of our fake staged fight at an award show.
我找到了我们在颁奖典礼上假装打架的所有照片。

852
00:40:44.680 --> 00:40:48.740
And then, you know, little things like I would text Steve.
还有，你知道的，我会给史蒂夫发些小消息之类的。

853
00:40:49.200 --> 00:40:53.800
I said, Steve, what did you do in your office when you were in there?
我问他：史蒂夫，你在办公室里的时候都做了些什么？

854
00:40:54.200 --> 00:40:55.900
All alone, as Michael Scott.
独自一人，以迈克尔·斯科特的身份。

855
00:40:56.140 --> 00:40:57.660
And he gave me little details.
他给了我一些小细节。

856
00:40:57.820 --> 00:41:00.280
So, I mean, it just, we can't thank people enough.
所以，我的意思是，我们真的非常感谢大家。

857
00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:04.440
And, Miguel, yes, we have definitely gone to our journals and old emails.
还有米格尔，是的，我们确实翻看了我们的日记和旧邮件。

858
00:41:04.620 --> 00:41:08.700
But what I realized in writing this book is the type of phones we had back then,
但我在写这本书时意识到，那时候我们用的手机，

859
00:41:08.840 --> 00:41:10.560
you didn't really text each other as much.
大家其实并不怎么发短信。

860
00:41:10.720 --> 00:41:11.740
Remember, it wasn't as easy.
记得吗，那时候没那么方便。

861
00:41:11.740 --> 00:41:16.700
So, what we would do is we would send each other, like, email updates about our week, our day.
所以，我们当时会互相发送关于那一周、那一天的邮件更新。

862
00:41:16.940 --> 00:41:18.380
We found so many of those.
我们找到了好多那样的邮件。

863
00:41:18.520 --> 00:41:21.340
Jenna, remember the amazing one Naomi sent?
珍娜，还记得娜奥米发来的那封神奇的邮件吗？

864
00:41:21.560 --> 00:41:21.920
Yes.
记得。

865
00:41:22.100 --> 00:41:26.940
My manager, Naomi Odenkirk, when we were writing our chapter, Death Bus,
我的经纪人娜奥米·奥登柯克，在我们写“死亡巴士”那一章时，

866
00:41:28.780 --> 00:41:31.980
about how the entire cast of The Office almost died,
关于《办公室》全体演员差点丧命的那次经历，

867
00:41:33.680 --> 00:41:40.720
Naomi found an email that I had written her about the shoot day where we all almost died three times.
娜奥米找到了一封我当时写给她的邮件，记录了我们差点三次丧命的那天拍摄的情况。

868
00:41:41.380 --> 00:41:43.180
And she sent it to me.
她把它发给了我。

869
00:41:43.320 --> 00:41:45.140
And I was like, oh, my gosh.
我当时心想：天哪。

870
00:41:45.300 --> 00:41:46.700
It had so many details in it.
里面有好多细节。

871
00:41:46.760 --> 00:41:47.620
Things I didn't remember.
我都已经不记得了。

872
00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:48.320
Amazing.
太神奇了。

873
00:41:48.500 --> 00:41:51.140
I mean, hard to believe I didn't remember those details.
我是说，真不敢相信我竟然不记得那些细节了。

874
00:41:51.600 --> 00:41:52.980
But I hadn't.
但我确实不记得了。

875
00:41:53.160 --> 00:41:54.100
So, thank you, Naomi.
所以，谢谢你，娜奥米。

876
00:41:54.780 --> 00:41:57.100
So, yes, you guys, it took a village, basically.
所以，是的，伙计们，基本上是集众人之力才完成的。

877
00:41:57.400 --> 00:41:57.940
That's right.
没错。

878
00:41:57.940 --> 00:42:01.220
All right, final question before we go to our next break.
好了，进入下一次休息前的最后一个问题。

879
00:42:01.460 --> 00:42:04.560
We got a lot of questions about our friendship.
我们收到了很多关于我们友谊的问题。

880
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:06.480
This book is about our friendship.
这本书就是关于我们的友谊的。

881
00:42:07.080 --> 00:42:09.160
Ruth from Galt, California said,
来自加利福尼亚州加尔特的露丝问道：

882
00:42:09.680 --> 00:42:14.400
All right, have you guys ever had a big fight or drifted apart?
好的，你们俩有没有过大吵一架或者渐行渐远的时候？

883
00:42:15.040 --> 00:42:16.880
We got a lot of questions like this, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了很多这样的问题。

884
00:42:17.080 --> 00:42:21.500
People are like, listen, we know you're friends, but don't friendships have bumps in the road?
大家都在问：听着，我们知道你们是朋友，但友谊难道不会有磕磕绊绊吗？

885
00:42:21.660 --> 00:42:22.720
People want to hear about them.
人们想听听这些故事。

886
00:42:22.860 --> 00:42:23.860
Of course they do.
他们当然想听。

887
00:42:23.860 --> 00:42:31.540
Well, guys, we do write about this in the book because we did have a big time when we did drift apart.
好吧，伙计们，我们在书里确实写到了这一点，因为我们确实有过一段渐行渐远的时期。

888
00:42:31.980 --> 00:42:35.240
It was right after Angela had her daughter, Isabel.
那是在安吉拉生下女儿伊莎贝尔之后。

889
00:42:35.540 --> 00:42:39.320
We write about it in our chapter, big pregs, little pregs, fake pregs.
我们在“大孕妇、小孕妇、假孕妇”那一章里写到了这件事。

890
00:42:39.840 --> 00:42:42.360
Our lives were just going in two different directions.
我们的生活当时正朝着两个不同的方向发展。

891
00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:43.020
Yeah.
是的。

892
00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:45.700
Jenna was entering what I call the sexy life.
珍娜当时进入了我所说的“性感生活”阶段。

893
00:42:46.400 --> 00:42:48.460
And I was home with a newborn.
而我则带着新生儿待在家里。

894
00:42:48.760 --> 00:42:52.240
And I did not know how to be a good friend to someone with a newborn.
我当时不知道该如何做一个好朋友去对待一个有新生儿的人。

895
00:42:52.240 --> 00:42:56.880
I mean, you just sometimes, I don't know, you can't know till you're in it.
我是说，有时候你就是……我不知道，除非身处其中，否则你无法理解。

896
00:42:57.180 --> 00:43:03.940
And we talk about in the book this period of time when Angela was a parent and I was not yet a parent.
我们在书里谈到了安吉拉为人父母而我还没当妈妈的那段时期。

897
00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:08.520
And I think that was the point in our lives when we were most distant.
我觉得那是我们生活中最疏远的一段时光。

898
00:43:09.240 --> 00:43:13.100
We were most distant, but it was all sort of circumstance.
我们确实最疏远，但这完全是环境使然。

899
00:43:13.100 --> 00:43:14.540
It wasn't our heart.
并不是因为我们的心变了。

900
00:43:14.900 --> 00:43:15.620
That's right.
没错。

901
00:43:15.820 --> 00:43:17.680
You know, so we found our way back.
你知道，我们最终还是找到了回来的路。

902
00:43:17.680 --> 00:43:19.880
But, yeah, every friendship has bumps.
不过，确实，每段友谊都会有磕磕绊绊。

903
00:43:20.100 --> 00:43:23.900
I mean, even learning to build a company together, we've had bumps.
我的意思是，即使是学习如何一起创办公司，我们也经历过波折。

904
00:43:24.080 --> 00:43:29.440
Learning how to really and truly how to merge two very different working styles.
学习如何真正地、彻底地融合两种截然不同的工作风格。

905
00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:33.060
But at the same time, what we realize is how rich it is.
但与此同时，我们意识到这种经历有多么宝贵。

906
00:43:33.200 --> 00:43:38.260
Once we get through that bump and on the other side, we're so much the better for it.
一旦我们克服了那些困难，跨过那道坎，我们都会因此变得更好。

907
00:43:38.260 --> 00:43:43.860
Well, something that is interesting about when we have bumps or when we have conflicts.
嗯，关于我们遇到波折或冲突时，有一点很有趣。

908
00:43:44.220 --> 00:43:48.360
You know, Angela, you're my person that I vent to about everybody else.
你知道，安吉拉，你是我向别人倾诉时找的那个人。

909
00:43:48.580 --> 00:43:49.020
I know.
我知道。

910
00:43:49.140 --> 00:43:49.520
Same.
我也是。

911
00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:52.520
So if I'm frustrated with you.
所以如果我对你有意见的话。

912
00:43:52.940 --> 00:43:54.180
Oh, it's terrifying.
哦，那太可怕了。

913
00:43:54.600 --> 00:43:58.220
I have to just tell you because you're the person I tell everything to.
我必须直接告诉你，因为你是我什么都说的那个人。

914
00:43:58.600 --> 00:43:58.650
I know.
我知道。

915
00:43:58.980 --> 00:44:02.340
So we've had moments where I'm like, listen, I got to vent.
所以我们有过这样的时刻，我会说，听着，我得发泄一下。

916
00:44:02.760 --> 00:44:05.420
And here's what it is because it's probably me.
事情是这样的，因为问题可能出在我身上。

917
00:44:05.620 --> 00:44:07.400
But this thing is driving me crazy.
但这事儿快把我逼疯了。

918
00:44:07.400 --> 00:44:07.820
Right.
没错。

919
00:44:08.040 --> 00:44:09.220
Or likewise, I'll say that.
或者同样地，我也会这么说。

920
00:44:09.300 --> 00:44:11.260
Like, listen, I know I'm half of this, okay?
就像，听着，我知道这事儿我有一半责任，好吗？

921
00:44:11.420 --> 00:44:13.820
But the other half is you and we got to sort it out.
但另一半责任在你，我们得把它解决掉。

922
00:44:13.920 --> 00:44:14.260
Yes.
是的。

923
00:44:15.020 --> 00:44:16.700
But it's so true.
但这太真实了。

924
00:44:16.980 --> 00:44:19.520
I, you know, Josh knows our friendship so well.
我，你知道，乔什非常了解我们的友谊。

925
00:44:19.680 --> 00:44:25.100
And he's so thankful for it because you get hours of venting that he doesn't have to sort out.
他非常感激这一点，因为你省去了他好几个小时听我发泄的麻烦。

926
00:44:25.920 --> 00:44:29.500
And he often will say to me when we've had those bumps, he'll be like,
当我们遇到那些磕磕绊绊时，他经常会对我这么说，他会说：

927
00:44:29.680 --> 00:44:31.740
you got to sort it out with Jenna because you're not right.
你得和珍娜把事情解决好，因为你现在的状态不对。

928
00:44:31.940 --> 00:44:32.960
Like, you're not quite right.
就是，你有点不太对劲。

929
00:44:33.980 --> 00:44:38.810
Oh, well, guys, thank you so much for sending in your questions.
哦，好吧，各位，非常感谢你们发来的问题。

930
00:44:39.150 --> 00:44:40.570
We're going to take a break.
我们要休息一下。

931
00:44:40.570 --> 00:44:44.410
And when we come back, we are going to play an excerpt from our audio book.
回来之后，我们将播放一段我们的有声书片段。

932
00:44:44.690 --> 00:44:50.270
It's from the chapter Big Pregs, Little Pregs, Fake Pregs, which is pretty perfect because
它出自《大孕肚、小孕肚、假孕肚》这一章，这非常贴切，因为

933
00:44:50.270 --> 00:44:54.030
it's all about our real pregnancies and our fake pregnancies for the show.
这一章讲的都是我们现实中的怀孕经历以及剧中虚构的怀孕经历。

934
00:44:54.190 --> 00:44:56.710
And next week, we're going to be breaking down the delivery.
下周，我们将深入探讨分娩那一章。

935
00:44:56.710 --> 00:44:57.770
I like it.
我喜欢。

936
00:45:06.000 --> 00:45:06.860
Chapter 10.
第十章。

937
00:45:07.720 --> 00:45:11.280
Big Pregs, Little Pregs, Fake Pregs.
《大孕肚、小孕肚、假孕肚》。

938
00:45:11.840 --> 00:45:12.920
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

939
00:45:13.520 --> 00:45:17.580
Kate Flannery just walked in and she has a piano.
凯特·弗兰纳里刚走进来，她带着一架钢琴。

940
00:45:17.920 --> 00:45:20.720
I think she's going to play a song for us.
我想她要为我们弹奏一曲。

941
00:45:22.060 --> 00:45:27.760
Big Pregs, Little Pregs, Fake Pregs, Big Pregs.
大孕肚、小孕肚、假孕肚，大孕肚。

942
00:45:35.570 --> 00:45:35.870
Ow!
哎哟！

943
00:45:36.050 --> 00:45:37.170
That was so great.
太棒了。

944
00:45:37.330 --> 00:45:38.250
Oh, and now Kate's leaving.
哦，现在凯特要走了。

945
00:45:38.330 --> 00:45:38.670
Bye, Kate.
再见，凯特。

946
00:45:38.730 --> 00:45:39.150
Oh, bye.
哦，再见。

947
00:45:39.410 --> 00:45:41.290
She just has a piano on her hip.
她居然随身带着一架钢琴。

948
00:45:41.290 --> 00:45:42.790
Does she walk around like that?
她平时走路都这样吗？

949
00:45:42.930 --> 00:45:43.530
Maybe so.
也许吧。

950
00:45:43.730 --> 00:45:44.850
How talented is she?
她多有才华啊？

951
00:45:45.530 --> 00:45:50.590
What a great way to start this chapter because we couldn't write a book about our best friendship
这一章的开头真是太棒了，因为如果不分享我们是如何度过为人父母的过渡期的，

952
00:45:50.590 --> 00:45:54.750
without sharing about how we navigated our transitions into parenthood.
我们就没法写出一本关于我们至深友谊的书。

953
00:45:55.370 --> 00:45:59.970
As anyone with children can tell you, becoming a parent is life-altering.
正如任何有孩子的人都能告诉你的那样，为人父母是改变人生的经历。

954
00:46:00.550 --> 00:46:06.150
Schedules change, priorities change, and as a result, sometimes even friendships change.
时间表变了，优先事项变了，结果有时连友谊也变了。

955
00:46:06.650 --> 00:46:10.210
We definitely had some bumpy moments once we became moMs.
我们成为妈妈后，确实经历了一些坎坷时刻。

956
00:46:10.210 --> 00:46:14.710
We're going to give it to you straight, with all the details, because that's how we do
我们要直截了当地告诉你，提供所有细节，因为这就是我们的风格。

957
00:46:14.710 --> 00:46:14.890
it.
就是这样。

958
00:46:15.490 --> 00:46:21.310
Also, as you listen to the next chapter, be prepared to hear a lot about wedgies and bodily
另外，当你听下一章时，要做好听到很多关于内裤卡裆和体液内容的准备。

959
00:46:21.310 --> 00:46:21.810
fluids.
体液。

960
00:46:22.330 --> 00:46:23.310
You've been warned.
我已经提醒过你了。

961
00:46:25.600 --> 00:46:30.560
While shooting season four of The Office, I was pregnant in real life, but my character
在拍摄《办公室》第四季时，我在现实生活中怀孕了，但我饰演的角色安吉拉并没有怀孕。

962
00:46:30.560 --> 00:46:31.880
of Angela was not.
所以我不得不把肚子藏在各种奇怪的东西后面。

963
00:46:32.160 --> 00:46:35.560
So we had to hide my belly behind all kinds of crazy things.
在《办公室》第六季中，帕姆怀孕了，但我现实中并没有怀孕。

964
00:46:36.540 --> 00:46:41.660
In season six of The Office, Pam was pregnant, but I was not pregnant in real life.
我在剧中戴了一个假肚子，我们亲切地称之为“假孕肚”。

965
00:46:41.920 --> 00:46:46.460
I wore a prosthetic belly for the show that we affectionately called fake pregs.
在第八季中，安吉拉·马丁怀孕了，而我是那个戴假孕肚的人。

966
00:46:47.140 --> 00:46:52.240
In season eight, Angela Martin was pregnant, and I was the one who was fake pregs.
在第八季中，帕姆又怀孕了，但这一次我在现实生活中也怀孕了。

967
00:46:53.120 --> 00:46:59.040
In season eight, Pam gets pregnant again, but this time I was also pregnant in real life.
我们俩之间这种“真怀孕”和“假怀孕”的来回切换，

968
00:46:59.880 --> 00:47:03.980
This back and forth of one of us being real pregnant and one of us being fake pregnant
成了大家困惑的源头。

969
00:47:03.980 --> 00:47:06.580
became a source of confusion for everyone.
有一天在片场，我们的剧本主管维达从笔记中抬起头说：

970
00:47:07.260 --> 00:47:11.280
One day on set, our script supervisor, Veda, looked up from her notes and said,
“等等，谁是假怀孕，谁是真怀孕？”

971
00:47:11.660 --> 00:47:14.700
Wait, who is fake pregnant and who is real pregnant?
我们真假怀孕的历程，以及在此期间我们友谊的演变，就是本章的主题：《大孕肚、小孕肚、假孕肚》。

972
00:47:15.840 --> 00:47:20.280
The journey of our real and fake pregnancies and the way our friendship evolved during those
我先怀孕了。

973
00:47:20.280 --> 00:47:26.120
times is the subject of this chapter, Big Pregs, Little Pregs, Fake Pregs.
那是2007年的夏天。

974
00:47:27.240 --> 00:47:28.680
I got pregnant firSt.
当我发现自己怀孕时，我太兴奋了，迫不及待地想告诉珍娜。

975
00:47:28.960 --> 00:47:30.780
It was the summer of 2007.
我费了九牛二虎之力才忍住没在知道的第一时间给她打电话，但我希望能当面告诉她，所以我决定在午餐时告诉她。

976
00:47:31.520 --> 00:47:35.160
I was so excited when I found out, and I couldn't wait to tell Jenna.
因为我们通常在珍娜的拖车里一起吃午饭，我知道那是让她单独相处的最好机会。

977
00:47:35.680 --> 00:47:40.320
It took everything I had not to call her the second I knew, but I wanted to deliver the news
我一走进去，珍娜就开始滔滔不绝地讲她那只猫安迪的故事。

978
00:47:40.320 --> 00:47:43.480
in person, so I decided to tell her at our lunch.
这是午餐时间的常见话题。

979
00:47:44.440 --> 00:47:48.900
Since we usually ate lunch together in Jenna's trailer, I knew that was my best shot at getting
她的猫总是做些最疯狂的事情。

980
00:47:48.900 --> 00:47:49.460
her alone.
“天哪，亲爱的，听着。”

981
00:47:50.100 --> 00:47:54.380
As soon as I walked in, Jenna launched into a long story about her cat, Andy.
“今天早上我走进厨房时，所有的底柜都开着。”

982
00:47:54.800 --> 00:47:56.660
This was a common lunchtime subject.
“就像所有的柜子，亲爱的。”

983
00:47:56.760 --> 00:47:59.320
Her cat was always doing the craziest things.
这个故事讲了五分钟，伙计们。

984
00:47:59.780 --> 00:48:02.100
Oh my God, lady, listen to this.
珍娜很爱那只猫。

985
00:48:02.280 --> 00:48:06.180
When I went into my kitchen this morning, all the bottom cabinets were open.
长话短说，安迪学会了如何打开柜子。

986
00:48:06.340 --> 00:48:07.740
Like all of them, lady.
我听着，笑着听她的故事，然后等待着。

987
00:48:08.480 --> 00:48:10.920
This story went on for five minutes, you guys.
当她讲完时，我脱口而出：“我怀孕了！”

988
00:48:11.620 --> 00:48:13.080
Jenna loved that cat.
我隐约记得一声闷响和尖叫，然后在一阵史诗般的熊抱之后，珍娜大喊：

989
00:48:13.480 --> 00:48:16.700
Long story short, Andy had learned how to open the cabinets.
“你为什么让我没完没了地讲我的猫？”

990
00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:20.620
I listened, laughed at her story, and waited.
这很准确，但让我解释一下那声闷响。

991
00:48:21.180 --> 00:48:24.560
When she was finished, I blurted out, I'm pregnant!
我被提前送去吃午饭，因为我们当时正在拍摄不需要前台接待的戏份。

992
00:48:25.060 --> 00:48:30.500
I vaguely remember a thud and shrieking, and then after an epic bear hug, Jenna yelled,
等安吉拉到达我的拖车时，我已经吃完饭，起身做些运动了。

993
00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:33.520
Why did you let me go on and on about my cat?
我在拖车里放了五磅重的哑铃，偶尔会做做二头肌弯举或俯卧撑，

994
00:48:34.500 --> 00:48:37.560
This is accurate, but let me explain the thud.
并喊着锻炼口号。

995
00:48:38.080 --> 00:48:41.980
I had been sent to lunch early because we were shooting something that didn't involve
这就是那声闷响的由来。

996
00:48:41.980 --> 00:48:42.760
front reception.
我当时正在做俯卧撑，听到安吉拉说她怀孕了，我太震惊了，直接从俯卧撑姿势摔到了地板上。

997
00:48:43.160 --> 00:48:47.560
By the time Angela got to my trailer, I was finished eating and had gotten up to do some
所以那声闷响其实是我摔倒的声音。

998
00:48:47.560 --> 00:48:48.100
exercise.
我们当时都惊呆了。

999
00:48:48.860 --> 00:48:54.200
I kept five-pound weights in my trailer and would do bicep curls or push-ups from time to time and
那是一个非常特别的时刻。

1000
00:48:54.200 --> 00:48:55.060
called out a workout.
我们当时都不知道，这只是我们未来几年共同经历的许多怀孕时刻的开始。

1001
00:48:55.060 --> 00:48:56.960
I was trying, okay?
我当时在努力了，好吗？

1002
00:48:57.780 --> 00:49:02.540
So I was pumping iron and droning on about my cat as Angela listened patiently.
当时我正在举铁，一边听安吉拉耐心地听我唠叨我的猫。

1003
00:49:03.080 --> 00:49:05.800
Mid-curl, she told me she was pregnant.
举到一半时，她告诉我她怀孕了。

1004
00:49:05.800 --> 00:49:11.760
I dropped the weights to the ground, causing the loud thud, then screamed for joy and hugged
我把哑铃扔在地上，发出一声巨响，然后尖叫着欢呼，拥抱了

1005
00:49:11.760 --> 00:49:12.600
my best friend.
我最好的朋友。

1006
00:49:13.120 --> 00:49:16.540
Our production assistant knocked on the door to ask if everything was okay.
我们的制片助理敲门问是不是出什么事了。

1007
00:49:17.220 --> 00:49:17.780
Yes!
没事！

1008
00:49:17.980 --> 00:49:19.900
We yelled through our tears of joy.
我们含着喜悦的泪水大喊道。

1009
00:49:20.520 --> 00:49:23.520
I knew how very much Angela wanted a child.
我知道安吉拉有多么渴望有个孩子。

1010
00:49:23.840 --> 00:49:25.760
I knew she would make a wonderful mother.
我知道她会成为一位出色的母亲。

1011
00:49:26.200 --> 00:49:28.020
I was just so happy for her.
我真心为她感到高兴。

1012
00:49:29.120 --> 00:49:33.540
In the weeks ahead, I shared the news with the rest of the cast, crew, and writing staff.
在接下来的几周里，我把这个消息告诉了剧组的其他演员、工作人员和编剧团队。

1013
00:49:33.940 --> 00:49:35.500
Everyone was so excited.
大家都非常兴奋。

1014
00:49:35.800 --> 00:49:40.560
The writers started discussing how they might work the pregnancy into the show and what that
编剧们开始讨论如何把怀孕的情节融入剧中，以及这对

1015
00:49:40.560 --> 00:49:41.900
might mean for Angela Martin.
安吉拉·马丁意味着什么。

1016
00:49:42.460 --> 00:49:44.640
Then, something crazy happened.
然后，疯狂的事情发生了。

1017
00:49:45.060 --> 00:49:50.540
The entire television and movie-making industry shut down due to the writers' strike, and
整个电视和电影制作行业因为编剧大罢工而停摆，

1018
00:49:50.540 --> 00:49:51.800
our show went on hiatus.
我们的剧集也暂停拍摄了。

1019
00:49:52.440 --> 00:49:55.040
No one knew how long the writers' strike would laSt.
没人知道编剧罢工会持续多久。

1020
00:49:55.280 --> 00:49:58.960
We had already filmed the first part of season four, and I wasn't showing then.
我们已经拍完了第四季的前半部分，那时我还没显怀。

1021
00:49:59.480 --> 00:50:05.240
When we finally started production again, four months later, I was seven months pregnant.
四个月后，当我们终于恢复拍摄时，我已经怀孕七个月了。

1022
00:50:05.800 --> 00:50:08.760
I had a very obvious, very huge belly.
我的肚子已经非常明显，非常大了。

1023
00:50:10.220 --> 00:50:14.740
The characters and storylines of the show were meant to pick up right where we'd left off.
剧中的角色和故事情节本应从我们中断的地方继续发展。

1024
00:50:15.000 --> 00:50:18.360
There was no way Angela's character could be pregnant out of the blue.
安吉拉这个角色不可能毫无预兆地突然怀孕。

1025
00:50:18.880 --> 00:50:22.600
We knew we'd have to hide it, and for that, we had to get creative.
我们知道必须把肚子藏起来，为此我们得发挥创意。

1026
00:50:23.540 --> 00:50:28.000
Angela did a lot of scenes standing behind the copier or the ficus plant in the bullpen.
安吉拉拍了很多站在复印机或办公区榕树后面的戏。

1027
00:50:28.000 --> 00:50:31.720
My personal favorite belly hide was during dinner party.
我个人最喜欢的藏肚方式是在“晚宴派对”那一集。

1028
00:50:32.600 --> 00:50:36.180
Andy Bernard and Angela Martin arrive at Jan and Michael's party together.
